    <bpmn:process id="W_W472" name="W472. BOI/PEZA/LGU Tax Incentive Monitoring &amp; Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New store opening in an LGU with tax incentive program; new entity registration with BOI or PEZA; annual compliance review cycle; incentive expiration approaching
Frequency: ~2–3 new incentive registrations/year (as new stores open or entities qualify); quarterly compliance monitoring; annual reporting per incentive
Volume: Potentially 5–15 active incentive registrations across 5 entities and 200+ locations (varies based on qualifying entities and LGU programs)
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: Tax Accountant, Controller, CFO, VP Legal, Regulatory Officer, Treasury Manager
Source: workflow W472 — BOI/PEZA/LGU Tax Incentive Monitoring &amp; Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W472_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W472_Lane1" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W472_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W472_Start3" name="New store opening in an LGU with tax incentive program; new entity registration with BOI…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task4" name="Incentive opportunity identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Incentive opportunity identification: (a) When a new store location is selected (W116), Tax Accountant reviews the LGU&#x27;s investment incentive code — many LGUs offer property tax holidays, local business tax reductions, or streamlined permitting for new businesses; (b) when a new entity is being formed or a DC location is selected, Tax Accountant assesses BOI or PEZA registration eligibility; (c) Tax Accountant monitors CREATE Law implementing rules and BIR revenue regulations for new incentive categories; (d) annual: Tax Accountant conducts a full incentive landscape review for all 5 entities and 205+ locations
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–4 hours/review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task5" name="Registration and qualification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Registration and qualification: (a) For BOI: Tax Accountant prepares registration application — project description, investment amount, employment generation plan, economic impact; VP Legal reviews and submits; BOI processes registration (3–6 months); upon approval, Tax Accountant records ITH start date, duration, and conditions; (b) For PEZA: similar process with PEZA Economic Zone administration; requires physical location within a PEZA-declared zone; (c) For LGU: Tax Accountant coordinates with Regulatory Officer to include tax incentive applications in the new store LGU permitting process (W54); negotiate incentive terms with LGU Investment Promotions Office
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 10–20 hours/registration</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task6" name="Compliance monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Compliance monitoring: (a) Tax Accountant maintains incentive compliance register per entity/location: incentive type, registration number, start date, expiration date, reporting requirements, compliance conditions (e.g., minimum employment, minimum investment, local sourcing percentage); (b) quarterly: Tax Accountant verifies compliance with all active incentive conditions — if BuildRight Logistics, Inc. is BOI-registered with a minimum employment condition, quarterly headcount at DC locations is verified against the commitment; (c) system alerts Tax Accountant 6 months and 3 months before incentive expiration — enough lead time for renewal application or tax planning for reversion to standard rates
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task7" name="BIR filing integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BIR filing integration: (a) For entities with ITH: Tax Accountant files BIR quarterly income tax returns (1702Q) with zero or reduced tax due, attaching BOI/PEZA certificate as supporting document; system applies reduced tax rate in tax computation module (W90, W260); (b) for entities with 5% GIT: Tax Accountant files 5% GIT return in lieu of regular corporate income tax and local business tax; system must support dual tax computation — standard rate for non-qualifying entities and 5% GIT for qualifying entities; (c) for LGU incentive: local business tax computation (W54, W9A.16c) reflects reduced or zero LBT for qualifying locations
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Absorbed into existing tax filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task8" name="Transfer pricing impact assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Transfer pricing impact assessment: (a) If one entity (e.g., Logistics, Inc.) has an income tax holiday while another (Depot, Inc.) does not, transfer pricing (W235) must be documented to demonstrate arm&#x27;s-length pricing — BIR scrutinizes IC transactions between incentivized and non-incentivized entities under CREATE Law; (b) Tax Accountant and Treasury Manager review IC pricing rules (W305) annually to ensure IC service fees and goods pricing do not artificially shift profit to the incentivized entity; (c) documentation per W235 (Transfer Pricing Compliance) updated to include incentive status analysis
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task9" name="Incentive benefit tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Incentive benefit tracking: (a) Tax Accountant calculates and records tax savings per incentive per quarter: ITH savings = taxable income × standard CIT rate (25%) minus tax paid (0% during ITH); GIT savings = (standard CIT + LBT) minus 5% GIT paid; LGU savings = standard LBT minus actual LBT paid; (b) quarterly report to Controller and CFO: cumulative tax savings vs. projection, compliance status, upcoming expirations; (c) annual: CFO includes incentive benefit in management reporting (W35) — total tax optimization from active incentive management
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller / CFO
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task10" name="Expiration management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Expiration management: (a) 12 months before incentive expiration: Tax Accountant assesses renewal options — some incentives are non-renewable (ITH); others may convert to enhanced deductions (5% GIT after ITH expiry for BOI); (b) 6 months before: Tax Accountant prepares tax planning for reversion to standard rates — models the financial impact on entity-level and consolidated effective tax rate; (c) upon expiration: system updates entity tax rate to standard; BIR filing (W260) reflects standard computation; LGU LBT reverts to full rate; (d) if renewal is possible: Tax Accountant prepares renewal application with updated compliance documentation
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–8 hours/expiration event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W472_Task11" name="Audit readiness">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Audit readiness: (a) Tax Accountant maintains complete incentive documentation file per entity: registration certificate, approval letter, incentive terms, annual compliance reports filed with BOI/PEZA/LGU, quarterly benefit calculations, transfer pricing documentation; (b) file available for BIR tax audit (W77) — BIR specifically audits entities with tax incentives to verify compliance; (c) file available for Internal Audit review (W349 — Corporate Tax &amp; Statutory Reporting Audit)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Absorbed into documentation practices</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W472_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W472_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W472_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W472_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: Tax Accountant review and approval gate
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W472_Assoc14" sourceRef="W472_Annotation13" targetRef="W472_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
