    <bpmn:process id="W_W473" name="W473. BIR Electronic Invoicing System (EIS) API Transmission &amp; Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Sales transaction completed at POS (W5B), Ecommerce order invoice generated (W11/W19), B2B invoice generated (W8/W165/W166), or customer refund processed (W101)
Frequency: Real-time (at transaction completion) or near-real-time batch transmission (within 72-hour BIR mandate)
Volume: ~2.8M POS transactions, ~42.9K ecommerce orders, ~3.5M line items, and ~3,500 AR invoices monthly across the 5 entities
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: POS Cashier, Billing Clerk, IT System Administrator, BIR EIS Portal, Integration Middleware, External CAS Consultant
Source: workflow W473 — BIR Electronic Invoicing System (EIS) API Transmission &amp; Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W473_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W473_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W473_Lane2" name="POS System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W473_Lane3" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W473_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W473_Start5" name="Sales transaction completed at POS (W5B), Ecommerce order invoice generated (W11/W19)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W473_Task6" name="Data Capture and Schema Validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Data Capture and Schema Validation: Upon POS checkout or B2B invoicing, the ERP/POS validation engine checks for mandatory BIR fields (Buyer name, buyer TIN, address, product code, description, quantity, unit price, breakdown of VATable/Exempt/Zero-rated sales, VAT amount, and withholding tax); system formats the transaction details into a standard BIR JSON schema.
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W473_Task7" name="Digital Signing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Digital Signing: The ERP security module applies BuildRight&#x27;s digital certificate (secured in HSM/KeyVault) to sign the JSON payload, ensuring non-repudiation.
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): IT Admin
Duration: &lt; 1 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W473_Task8" name="API Transmission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: API Transmission: ERP transmission service calls the BIR EIS API endpoints (using secure TLS 1.2+ connection) to transmit the signed JSON payload.
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): IT Admin
Duration: &lt; 3 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W473_Task9" name="BIR Acknowledgment &amp; UUID Storage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BIR Acknowledgment &amp; UUID Storage: BIR EIS portal processes the payload, validates the schema, and returns a 200 OK response with a unique transaction reference key (UUID); ERP saves this UUID and receipt timestamp in the Local Invoice Registry linked to the original sales invoice/POS transaction.
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: &lt; 2 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W473_Task10" name="Transmission Exception Handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Transmission Exception Handling: If the transmission fails due to network outage, BIR portal downtime, or schema validation error: (a) system flags the transaction as &quot;Failed/Pending&quot;; (b) routes validation errors to the Billing Clerk for correction; (c) for network/portal issues, automatically retries every 30 minutes; (d) queues offline POS transactions for automatic transmission upon restoration.
Responsible (R): System / Billing Clerk
Accountable (A): Tax Accountant
Duration: Automated / Varies</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W473_Task11" name="Fulfillment &amp; Customer Copy Delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Fulfillment &amp; Customer Copy Delivery: Once the UUID is received (or queued in offline mode), the POS prints the BIR-compliant receipt with a QR code containing the BIR validation link; or the ecommerce system emails the e-invoice to the customer.
Responsible (R): POS System / Ecommerce Engine
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: &lt; 5 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W473_Task12" name="Daily Reconciliation &amp; Audit Log Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Daily Reconciliation &amp; Audit Log Review: Tax Accountant runs the e-Invoicing Transmission Report daily: compares total sales invoice count from the General Ledger (W9A) and POS sales reports against the transmitted/accepted records in the Local Invoice Registry; flags and investigates any transactions pending transmission or rejected by BIR.
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W473_Task13" name="BIR e-Invoicing Compliance Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: BIR e-Invoicing Compliance Reporting: Tax Accountant prepares monthly EIS compliance summaries, verifying that all sales records are fully accounted for in the BIR portal before filing monthly VAT returns (W90/W260).
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W473_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W473_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W473_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W473_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: Tax Accountant review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W473_Assoc16" sourceRef="W473_Annotation15" targetRef="W473_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
