    <bpmn:process id="W_W590" name="W590. Monthly Tax Provision &amp; Compliance Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Month-end close process initiation (day 1 of following month), feeds into W9 financial close
Frequency: Monthly (by day 3 of following month, to meet 5-day month-end close target)
Volume: 5 legal entities; monthly tax provisions covering: VAT (12% on ~PHP 5.19B monthly revenue), EWT (1–10% on ~PHP 2.5B monthly AP), CWT collection (~PHP 300M/month in customer CWT), percentage tax (3% on VAT-exempt revenue streams), corporate income tax (RCIT 25% / FCIT 20% per CREATE law per PAS 12), local taxes (LGU business tax quarterly); BIR eFPS filing deadlines per tax type
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: Tax Accountant, Chief Accountant, Controller (A for provision approval), AP Supervisor (C for EWT data), AR Supervisor (C for CWT data), Treasury Analyst (C for tax payment funding), External Tax Advisor (C for complex positions)
Source: workflow W590 — Monthly Tax Provision &amp; Compliance Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W590_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W590_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W590_Lane2" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W590_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W590_Start4" name="Month-end close process initiation (day 1 of following month), feeds into W9 financial…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W590_Task5" name="Revenue-based tax provision computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Revenue-based tax provision computation: System auto-computes tax provisions based on month&#x27;s posted revenue per entity — (a) Output VAT (12%): gross revenue per entity from POS (Depot Inc.), ecommerce (Digital Commerce Inc.), services (Logistics Inc., Property Mgmt Inc.), and management fees (Holdings Inc.); separately identify VAT-exempt sales (senior citizen/PWD per W217, agricultural products, residential lease below threshold) which are subject to percentage tax (3%) instead; (b) Percentage tax (3%): computed on VAT-exempt revenue streams per W499; (c) Gross receipts tax: applicable to financial income and certain service revenues per entity; (d) LGU business tax accrual: quarterly LGU payments accrued monthly based on prior year&#x27;s assessed business tax per LGU per entity
Responsible (R): System / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 30 min (review automated computation)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task6" name="VAT input/output reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VAT input/output reconciliation: Tax Accountant reconciles VAT position per entity — (a) Output VAT: total output VAT from sales invoices and official receipts per BIR EIS transmission log (W473); include output VAT on deemed sales (IC transfers between VAT-registered entities per W14); verify output VAT on importations (customs-assessed VAT per W239); (b) Input VAT: total input VAT from purchase invoices (domestic), import customs declarations, and other creditable input VAT; verify input VAT claims are supported by valid VAT invoices/official receipts per BIR requirements; identify deferred input VAT (purchases recorded but VAT invoice not yet received from vendor); (c) Net VAT payable/receivable: output VAT minus input VAT per entity; if net payable, this is the amount due for BIR 2550M filing; if net receivable (excess input VAT from imports or capital goods), determine whether to claim refund (BIR processing time 12–24 months) or carry forward to next month per W90; (d) VAT reconciliation exceptions: unmatched input VAT claims (vendor VAT invoice received but purchase not yet posted), missing VAT invoices from vendors, VAT rate discrepancies (10% vs. 12% transition period issues for older invoices)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 60 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task7" name="EWT remittance reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: EWT remittance reconciliation: Tax Accountant reconciles EWT per entity — (a) pull EWT amounts withheld from AP module: EWT rates applied per vendor/payee type — 1% (corporate suppliers of goods per RR 2-98 as amended), 2% (corporate suppliers of services), 5–10% (individual payees per tax table), 10% (professionals); (b) compare to EWT amounts remitted via BIR eFPS per BIR Form 1601-EQ; (c) identify discrepancies: under-remittance (withholding deducted from vendor but not remitted to BIR = company liability), over-remittance (remitted more than withheld = requires reconciliation with vendor); (d) verify EWT certificate (BIR 2306/2307) generation per W475 — certificates must be issued to vendors within 20 days of quarter close per BIR requirement (RR 11-2018)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task8" name="CWT certificate collection status review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: CWT certificate collection status review: Tax Accountant reviews CWT certificates collected from customers — (a) pull list of customers who withheld tax on payments to BuildRight during the month (primarily B2B corporate customers and government entities); (b) verify BIR Form 2307 certificates received from customers — required to credit CWT against quarterly income tax per BIR 1702Q; (c) follow up on missing certificates with AR Supervisor — customer contact per W8 for certificate collection; (d) compute total CWT available as tax credit for current quarter; (e) flag material uncollected CWT (&gt;PHP 1M per customer) for escalation to Credit Manager
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task9" name="Deferred tax movement computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Deferred tax movement computation: Tax Accountant computes deferred tax movements per PAS 12 per entity — (a) Temporary differences: depreciation timing (tax vs. book per W407 — accelerated depreciation for tax vs. straight-line for book), accrued expenses not yet deductible (provisions requiring cash basis recognition per BIR), unrealized FX gains/losses; (b) Deferred tax liability (DTL): taxable temporary differences × applicable rate (25% RCIT for domestic corporations per CREATE Law; ROHCs are also at 25% under CREATE); (c) Deferred tax asset (DTA): deductible temporary differences × applicable rate, including net operating loss carryover (NOLCO) per CREATE — NOLCO carryforward period is 3 consecutive years, extended to 5 years for FY2020–2021 losses of non-large taxpayers per CREATE (RR 25-2020); (d) DTL/DTA movement: current month movement = ending balance minus beginning balance; movement posted to deferred tax provision journal entry
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task10" name="Tax provision journal entry preparation and posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Tax provision journal entry preparation and posting: Tax Accountant prepares composite tax provision journal entry per entity — (a) Output VAT provision: debit VAT output (liability), credit VAT payable; (b) Input VAT claim: debit VAT input (asset), credit VAT expense/VAT payable; (c) EWT payable: debit EWT expense (embedded in purchase cost), credit EWT payable; (d) CWT receivable: debit CWT receivable (asset), credit income tax provision; (e) Current income tax provision: debit income tax expense, credit current income tax payable (estimated based on quarterly-to-date taxable income); (f) Deferred tax provision: debit/credit deferred tax expense, credit/debit DTL/DTA per step 5; (g) Percentage tax payable: debit percentage tax expense, credit percentage tax payable; (h) LGU business tax accrual: debit LGU tax expense, credit LGU tax payable (accrual); Tax Accountant posts journal entries in ERP; Chief Accountant reviews and approves before close completion
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 45 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task11" name="Tax compliance calendar review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Tax compliance calendar review: Tax Accountant reviews 30-day forward compliance calendar — (a) BIR 2550M (Monthly VAT Return): due 20th of following month or 25th via eFPS per W90; (b) BIR 1601-EQ (Quarterly EWT Remittance Return): due last day of the month following quarter close via eFPS per W260; (c) BIR 1601-C (Monthly CWT Remittance Return): due 10th of following month via eFPS; (d) BIR 1702Q (Quarterly Income Tax Return): due 60 days after quarter-end (if current month is quarter-end); (e) BIR 1604-E/1604-C (Annual Information Returns): due January 31 of following year (if applicable); (f) LGU business tax: quarterly payments per LGU schedule (varies by city/municipality where 5 entities are registered); (g) BIR EIS transmission: daily sales invoice transmission per W473 — verify no gaps in transmission log; (h) Tax Accountant confirms all deadlines are tracked in compliance calendar with responsible person assigned and preparation start date flagged
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task12" name="BIR filing preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: BIR filing preparation: Tax Accountant prepares upcoming month BIR filings — (a) pre-populate BIR 2550M from system VAT reconciliation (step 2); (b) pre-populate BIR 1601-EQ from system EWT reconciliation (step 3); (c) pre-populate BIR 1601-C from system CWT reconciliation (step 4); (d) verify tax amounts match provision journal entries (step 6); (e) generate draft returns for Chief Accountant review; (f) Chief Accountant reviews and approves draft returns; (g) Tax Accountant submits via BIR eFPS per W260
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task13" name="LGU tax payments review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: LGU tax payments review: Tax Accountant reviews LGU tax obligations — (a) verify quarterly LGU business tax payments are accrued correctly per entity per LGU jurisdiction; (b) confirm payments to LGUs where entities hold business permits (Quezon City, Manila, Laguna, Clark, Cebu — per entity registration); (c) verify real property tax (RPT) semi-annual payments per W184 for owned properties; (d) confirm LGU tax payments are scheduled in cash flow forecast per W589
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Chief Accountant
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W590_Task14" name="Quarterly income tax provision review (if quarter-end month)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Quarterly income tax provision review (if quarter-end month): If current month is quarter-end (March, June, September, December), Tax Accountant conducts comprehensive quarterly review — (a) compute cumulative quarterly taxable income per entity per BIR 1702Q; (b) reconcile cumulative tax provision (current + deferred) to estimated annual tax liability; (c) adjust quarterly provision if material variance between estimated annual tax and year-to-date provision; (d) verify NOLCO utilization per CREATE Law provisions; (e) review tax incentives per W472 (BOI/PEZA registered activities if applicable); (f) External Tax Advisor reviews complex positions (cross-border, transfer pricing per W486, related party transactions per PAS 24)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / External Tax Advisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours (quarterly)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W590_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W590_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W590_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W590_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: Chief Accountant review and approval of the monthly tax provision journal entries and draft BIR returns before close completion
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W590_Assoc17" sourceRef="W590_Annotation16" targetRef="W590_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow18" sourceRef="W590_Start4" targetRef="W590_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow19" sourceRef="W590_Task5" targetRef="W590_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow20" sourceRef="W590_Task6" targetRef="W590_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow21" sourceRef="W590_Task7" targetRef="W590_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow22" sourceRef="W590_Task8" targetRef="W590_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow23" sourceRef="W590_Task9" targetRef="W590_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow24" sourceRef="W590_Task10" targetRef="W590_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow25" sourceRef="W590_Task11" targetRef="W590_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow26" sourceRef="W590_Task12" targetRef="W590_Task13" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow27" sourceRef="W590_Task13" targetRef="W590_Task14" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W590_Flow28" sourceRef="W590_Task14" targetRef="W590_End15" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W590_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W590_plane" bpmnElement="W_W590">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W590_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W590_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2420" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
