    <bpmn:process id="W_W711" name="W711. BIR Withholding Tax (EWT) Certificate Form 2307 Issuance to Vendors" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarter-end EWT remittance cycle (BIR Form 1601-EQ per W260); or vendor requests BIR Form 2307 for their own tax credit claim (issued immediately upon written request)
Frequency: Quarterly (batch issuance, due on or before the 20th day of the month following quarter close per RR 11-2018); ad-hoc per vendor request
Volume: ~800–1,000 vendor EWT certificates per quarter (one per vendor with EWT transactions in the quarter); ~3,200–4,000 per year
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: AP Clerk, Finance Manager, Vendor, BIR
Source: workflow W711 — BIR Withholding Tax (EWT) Certificate Form 2307 Issuance to Vendors</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W711_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W711_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W711_Lane2" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W711_Lane3" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W711_Lane4" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W711_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W711_Start6" name="Quarter-end EWT remittance cycle (BIR Form 1601-EQ per W260); or vendor requests BIR Form…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W711_Task7" name="Quarterly EWT extraction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly EWT extraction: after the quarter&#x27;s AP payment runs per W556, system extracts all EWT transactions for the quarter grouped by vendor: vendor TIN, vendor name, ATC (Alphanumeric Tax Code), gross amount, EWT rate, EWT amount withheld, payment date, PO/invoice reference
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Tax Accountant
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W711_Task8" name="2307 batch generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: 2307 batch generation: system generates BIR Form 2307 for each vendor with EWT transactions during the quarter: (a) Part I — Payor info (BuildRight legal name, TIN, address, registered address per BIR registration); (b) Part II — Payee info (vendor name, TIN, registered address); (c) Part III — Details of income payments and taxes withheld during the quarter: date of payment, ATC, nature of income payment, gross amount, EWT rate, EWT amount; (d) Part IV — total amount withheld; (e) system auto-calculates totals and validates against AP EWT ledger
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Tax Accountant
Duration: Batch: 2-3 hours for ~1,000 forms</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W711_Task9" name="Validation and review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Validation and review: Tax Accountant reviews batch: (a) verify vendor TIN format matches BIR registration (XXX-XXX-XXX or XXX-XXX-XXX-XXX); (b) verify ATC codes are correct per income nature (e.g., WC 010 for professional/technical services to corporate vendors at 2%, WI 010 for rentals at 5%, WP 010 for purchases of goods at 1%); (c) verify EWT rates match ATC code requirements; (d) check for duplicate vendor entries or missing vendor data; (e) flag exceptions for manual correction
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 2-3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W711_Task10" name="Approval and signing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Approval and signing: Finance Manager reviews summary report: total EWT certificates generated, total EWT amounts per ATC category, reconciliation against BIR Form 1601-EQ quarterly remittance per W260; approves batch for issuance; authorized signatory (Finance Manager or Controller) signs certificates
Responsible (R): Finance Manager
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30-60 min/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W711_Task11" name="Distribution to vendors">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Distribution to vendors: system distributes Form 2307 to vendors: (a) primary: email PDF to vendor&#x27;s registered email address from vendor master; (b) secondary: upload to vendor self-service portal per W705 for vendor download; (c) physical mail for vendors without email (rare); (d) system logs distribution date and method per certificate
Responsible (R): System / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Tax Accountant
Duration: Automated + 1 hour/quarter for physical mail exceptions</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W711_Task12" name="Quarterly reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly reconciliation: at quarter-end, Tax Accountant reconciles: (a) total EWT certificates issued (quarterly sum of Forms 2307) vs. total EWT remitted to BIR per Form 1601-EQ filing; (b) any unreconciled difference investigated and corrected; (c) vendor-level reconciliation: verify every vendor with EWT deduction received their 2307; (d) BIR Form 1604-E (Annual Information Return of Income Payments Subject to WHT) preparation uses 2307 data as primary source
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 4-6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W711_Task13" name="Ad-hoc vendor request handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Ad-hoc vendor request handling: when a vendor requests a copy or re-issuance of their Form 2307: (a) AP Clerk verifies vendor identity (TIN + registered business name); (b) system retrieves historical 2307 from document archive per W255; (c) re-issue via email or portal download; (d) if vendor disputes EWT amount: Tax Accountant investigates against AP transaction history and resolves per W244 (vendor invoice dispute)
Responsible (R): AP Clerk / Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Accountant
Duration: 15-30 min per request; ~20–30 ad-hoc requests/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W711_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W711_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W711_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W711_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: Tax Accountant review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W711_Assoc16" sourceRef="W711_Annotation15" targetRef="W711_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
