    <bpmn:process id="W_W1418" name="W1418. Multi-Entity Consolidated VAT Input-Output Reconciliation, Monthly BIR 2550M Filing &amp; Credit Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly VAT filing deadline (20th of the following month per BIR requirement)
Frequency: Monthly per entity (5 entities × 12 months = 60 filings/year); quarterly consolidated reconciliation
Volume: ~PHP 62.3B annual revenue × 12% VAT = ~PHP 7.5B output VAT/year; ~PHP 42–45B COGS × 12% VAT = ~PHP 5.0–5.4B input VAT/year; net VAT payable ~PHP 2.1–2.5B/year across 5 entities
Owner: Tax Accountant
Participants: Tax Accountant, AP Clerk, AR Clerk, Controller, BIR eFPS Administrator
Source: workflow W1418 — Multi-Entity Consolidated VAT Input-Output Reconciliation, Monthly BIR 2550M Filing &amp; Credit Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1418_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1418_Lane1" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1418_Lane2" name="BIR eFPS Administrator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1418_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1418_Start4" name="Monthly VAT filing deadline (20th of the following month per BIR requirement)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1418_Task5" name="Monthly output VAT reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly output VAT reconciliation: Tax Accountant reconciles output VAT per entity: (a) POS sales VAT: system-generated output VAT from POS transactions (2.8M transactions) × 12%, (b) trade account sales VAT: from AR invoices (~3,500/month) × 12%, (c) ecommerce sales VAT: from online transactions (~42,900/month) × 12%, (d) intercompany sales VAT: IC transactions between entities, (e) exempt sales identified and excluded (if any), (f) total output VAT per entity reconciled to GL VAT payable account
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4–6 hours/entity/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1418_Task6" name="Monthly input VAT reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly input VAT reconciliation: Tax Accountant reconciles input VAT per entity: (a) merchandise AP invoices: input VAT from vendor invoices with valid BIR-registered VAT receipts, (b) import VAT: from customs import entries (duties and VAT paid at port per W144/W1233), (c) operating expense invoices: input VAT from non-trade vendors (rent, utilities, services), (d) intercompany purchase VAT: IC transactions from other entities, (e) validation: verify all input VAT claims have supporting BIR-registered VAT invoices/invoices with TIN; exclude invalid claims, (f) total input VAT per entity reconciled to GL VAT receivable account
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4–6 hours/entity/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1418_Task7" name="Net VAT computation and 2550M preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Net VAT computation and 2550M preparation: (a) per entity: compute net VAT payable = output VAT − input VAT carryforward from prior month − current month input VAT, (b) apply 70% input VAT limitation rule if applicable, (c) compute unutilized input VAT carryforward to next month, (d) prepare BIR Form 2550M per entity: sales/receipts, purchases, output VAT, input VAT, net VAT payable, (e) Controller reviews 5 entity returns before filing
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/entity/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1418_Task8" name="BIR eFPS filing and payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BIR eFPS filing and payment: (a) BIR eFPS Administrator files 5 monthly VAT returns via BIR Electronic Filing and Payment System, (b) generate payment instructions for net VAT payable per entity per bank account, (c) Treasury releases VAT payments via bank channel per W34, (d) file confirmation and payment receipts saved as supporting documentation
Responsible (R): BIR eFPS Administrator / Treasury
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1418_Task9" name="Quarterly consolidated VAT reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly consolidated VAT reconciliation: (a) Consolidation Accountant reconciles consolidated VAT: eliminate intercompany input/output VAT (net zero in consolidation), (b) verify consolidated net VAT = sum of entity net VAT payable to BIR, (c) review input VAT utilization rate by entity: identify entities with large input VAT carryforward (potential cash flow inefficiency — cash tied up in VAT credits), (d) report to CFO on quarterly VAT position
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant / Consolidation Accountant
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1418_Task10" name="Annual VAT reconciliation (BIR 2550Q)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual VAT reconciliation (BIR 2550Q): (a) quarterly summary of monthly filings per entity, (b) annual true-up: verify full-year input VAT claims vs. audited financial statements, (c) prepare BIR Form 2550Q (Quarterly VAT Return) per entity per quarter, (d) coordinate with external tax advisor for any complex VAT issues (e.g., PEZA transactions, zero-rated sales, VAT-exempt items)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 8–12 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1418_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1418_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1418_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1418_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: Tax Accountant review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Tax Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1418_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1418_Annotation12" targetRef="W1418_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1418_Flow14" sourceRef="W1418_Start4" targetRef="W1418_Task5" />
