    <bpmn:process id="W_W1503" name="W1503. BIR Percentage Tax vs. VAT Threshold Monitoring, Quarterly Tax Regime Evaluation &amp; Registration Adjustment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly rolling 12-month gross sales calculation; quarterly tax regime evaluation; BIR registration update required when crossing VAT threshold (PHP 3M annual gross sales)
Frequency: Monthly monitoring; quarterly evaluation; per-entity registration adjustment as needed
Volume: 5 legal entities; BuildRight Depot, Inc. and BuildRight Logistics, Inc. are well above threshold; BuildRight Digital Commerce, Inc. and newer entities may fluctuate near threshold
Owner: Tax Manager
Participants: Tax Manager, Intercompany Accountant, CFO, BIR RDO (Revenue District Office)
Source: workflow W1503 — BIR Percentage Tax vs. VAT Threshold Monitoring, Quarterly Tax Regime Evaluation &amp; Registration Adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1503_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1503_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1503_Lane2" name="Tax Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1503_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1503_Start4" name="Monthly rolling 12-month gross sales calculation; quarterly tax regime evaluation; BIR…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1503_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1503_Task5" name="Monthly rolling 12-month gross sales tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly rolling 12-month gross sales tracking: Monthly: (a) system calculates rolling 12-month gross sales per legal entity: (i) BuildRight Holdings, Inc. (investment income only — exempt from VAT on certain investment returns); (ii) BuildRight Depot, Inc. (retail sales — well above threshold); (iii) BuildRight Logistics, Inc. (service fees — above threshold); (iv) BuildRight Digital Commerce, Inc. (ecommerce service fees — may be near threshold); (v) BuildRight Property Management, Inc. (rental income — above threshold); (b) for entities near the PHP 3M threshold (within 20%): (i) system projects forward based on current monthly run rate; (ii) if projected to exceed within 3 months: alert sent to Tax Manager; (c) results reported to CFO monthly as part of tax compliance dashboard
Responsible (R): System / Intercompany Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1503_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1503_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1503_Task6" name="Quarterly tax regime evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly tax regime evaluation: Quarterly: (a) Tax Manager evaluates for each entity near threshold: (i) actual gross sales for the trailing 12 months; (ii) forward 12-month projection based on growth trend; (iii) upcoming large contracts or revenue events that could push the entity over threshold; (iv) whether percentage tax or VAT is more economically advantageous for the entity (for entities below threshold, percentage tax may be cheaper but VAT registration allows input tax claims); (b) recommendation: (i) remain on percentage tax — entity clearly below threshold; (ii) voluntary VAT registration — entity approaching threshold, better to register early and claim input tax credits; (iii) mandatory VAT registration — entity has exceeded or will exceed threshold within the quarter; (c) recommendation presented to CFO for decision
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1503_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1503_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1503_Task7" name="BIR VAT registration application">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: BIR VAT registration application: If entity crosses threshold or voluntarily registers for VAT: (a) Tax Manager prepares BIR registration update: (i) BIR Form 1905 (Registration Data Update); (ii) certification of gross sales exceeding PHP 3M (or voluntary registration intent); (iii) updated Articles of Incorporation or proof of business registration; (b) submits to the BIR RDO where the entity is registered; (c) BIR processes update (typically 10–15 business days); (d) entity receives updated Certificate of Registration (COR) reflecting VAT status; (e) Tax Manager updates the entity&#x27;s tax profile in the ERP system: (i) tax classification changed from &quot;Non-VAT&quot; to &quot;VAT&quot;; (ii) sales invoice format updated to include VAT breakdown; (iii) purchasing enabled for VAT input tax tracking; (f) all downstream processes updated: invoicing, purchasing, reporting
Responsible (R): Tax Manager / BIR RDO
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 5–10 business days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1503_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1503_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1503_Task8" name="Transition period compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Transition period compliance: During transition from percentage tax to VAT: (a) Tax Manager ensures: (i) all sales from the VAT registration effective date forward include 12% VAT; (ii) existing inventory at time of transition: input tax credit claim filed for VAT paid on inventory purchased before registration (as allowed under BIR rules); (iii) percentage tax returns filed for the final period before VAT registration; (iv) first VAT return filed for the period starting from registration date; (v) books of accounts updated to reflect VAT accounting; (b) any customer-facing documentation updated: (i) official receipts reprinted with VAT details; (ii) sales invoices reformatted; (iii) POS terminals reconfigured to apply VAT
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1503_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1503_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1503_Task9" name="Continuous monitoring &amp; threshold re-evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Continuous monitoring &amp; threshold re-evaluation: (a) Tax Manager monitors for: (i) entities whose gross sales decline below PHP 3M — under current law, once VAT-registered, the entity remains VAT-registered unless it applies for cancellation (complex process rarely pursued); (ii) new BIR issuances that may change the threshold or rules; (iii) proposed tax reforms (e.g., CREATE MORE Act) that may adjust the threshold; (b) if threshold rules change: impact analysis on all 5 entities within 30 days of new law/issuance
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1503_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1503_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1503_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1503_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1503_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: reconfiguration — all within a tight compliance timeline
Owner: Tax Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1503_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1503_Annotation11" targetRef="W1503_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1503_Flow13" sourceRef="W1503_Start4" targetRef="W1503_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1503_Flow14" sourceRef="W1503_Task5" targetRef="W1503_Task6" />
