    <bpmn:process id="W_W1525" name="W1525. Philippine BIR Computerized Accounting System (CAS) Registration, Permit Renewal &amp; Annual Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Initial ERP system implementation requiring BIR CAS registration, (b) annual CAS permit renewal, (c) system upgrade or migration requiring re-registration
Frequency: Initial registration (one-time per system); annual renewal; ad-hoc for system changes
Volume: 5 legal entities × CAS registration = 5 registrations; annual renewal for all 5
Owner: Tax Compliance Manager
Participants: Tax Compliance Manager, IT ERP Team, Finance Controller, external tax counsel, BIR Revenue District Office (RDO)
Source: workflow W1525 — Philippine BIR Computerized Accounting System (CAS) Registration, Permit Renewal &amp; Annual Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1525_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1525_Lane1" name="Tax Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1525_Lane2" name="IT ERP Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1525_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1525_Start4" name="(a) Initial ERP system implementation requiring BIR CAS registration, (b) annual CAS…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1525_Task5" name="Initial CAS registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Initial CAS registration (for new entity or system): (a) Tax Compliance Manager prepares registration documents per BIR RDO requirements: (i) BIR Form 1907 (Application for Registration of CAS/Components), (ii) system description: name, version, developer, modules (GL, AP, AR, inventory, POS), hardware configuration, data security measures, (iii) sample printouts of all books of accounts (cash receipts journal, cash disbursements journal, sales journal, purchases journal, general journal, subsidiary ledgers), (iv) sample official receipts and sales invoices generated by the system, (v) affidavit of responsible officer attesting to system accuracy and integrity, (vi) sworn statement on data retention and backup procedures; (b) Finance Controller and IT ERP Team provide technical specifications; (c) external tax counsel reviews documentation package
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager / IT ERP Team
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 weeks preparation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1525_Task6" name="BIR submission and demonstration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: BIR submission and demonstration: (a) Tax Compliance Officer submits documentation to the BIR Revenue District Office (RDO) where each entity is registered; (b) BIR may require a system demonstration: (i) Tax Compliance Manager and IT ERP Team present system at BIR office, (ii) demonstrate: transaction recording, report generation, books of accounts generation, invoice/receipt generation, data retention and backup; (c) BIR evaluates system against checklist: (i) compliance with Philippine account code structure, (ii) ability to generate required BIR reports, (iii) audit trail integrity (no backdating, no deletion without log), (iv) data retention capability (10 years per NIRC — Sec. 235, as amended by TRAIN RA 10963; BuildRight targets 10 years per A6.5)
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager / IT ERP Team
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours demonstration + 2–4 weeks BIR processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1525_Task7" name="PTU issuance and implementation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: PTU issuance and implementation: (a) BIR issues Permit to Use (PTU) for each entity&#x27;s CAS; (b) Tax Compliance Manager files PTU with entity&#x27;s BIR registration records; (c) PTU number referenced on all BIR filings going forward; (d) system configuration updated: PTU number displayed on system-generated reports per BIR requirement
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1525_Task8" name="Annual PTU renewal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Annual PTU renewal: (a) Tax Compliance Manager prepares renewal application 60 days before PTU expiry: (i) updated system description (if any changes), (ii) certification that no unauthorized modifications have been made, (iii) updated sample printouts if report formats changed; (b) submits renewal to RDO; (c) if BIR requests system re-demonstration: coordinates with IT ERP Team; (d) renews PTU and updates records
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1–2 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1525_Task9" name="System change notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System change notification: (a) when IT ERP Team plans system changes that affect CAS: (i) ERP version upgrade, (ii) new module activation (e.g., adding WMS module, POS module replacement), (iii) chart of accounts restructuring, (iv) database migration, (v) change in invoice/receipt format; (b) IT ERP Team notifies Tax Compliance Manager before implementation; (c) Tax Compliance Manager assesses: (i) minor changes (bug fixes, UI updates): no BIR notification needed, (ii) moderate changes (new module, report format change): BIR notification letter within 30 days, (iii) major changes (system replacement, database migration): re-registration per Steps 1–3; (d) external tax counsel advises on classification of change
Responsible (R): IT ERP Team / Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1–5 days depending on change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1525_Task10" name="Annual compliance audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual compliance audit: (a) Tax Compliance Manager performs annual CAS compliance self-check: (i) system continues to generate all required BIR books of accounts accurately, (ii) audit trail is intact (no unauthorized modifications), (iii) data retention meets 10-year requirement, (iv) all 5 entity PTUs are current and valid, (v) any system changes during the year were properly notified to BIR; (b) documents compliance status for Finance Controller review; (c) any gaps remediated before BIR audit exposure
Responsible (R): Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 4–6 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1525_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1525_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1525_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1525_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: Tax Compliance Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Tax Compliance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1525_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1525_Annotation12" targetRef="W1525_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
