    <bpmn:process id="W_W5530" name="W5530. Minimum Corporate Income Tax (MCIT) Computation, Regime Evaluation &amp; 3-Year Excess-Credit Carry-Forward" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly close (W9A) and the annual income-tax-return cycle (W407/W90 calendar); an entity&#x27;s 4th taxable year beginning (MCIT applicability onset per NIRC §27(E)/§28(A)(e)); a loss year or business-reversal event raising the relief question; or an entity entering the 3-year excess-credit window
Frequency: Quarterly evaluation per entity; annual computation and return integration; event-driven applicability/relief reviews
Volume: 5 legal entities × 4 quarterly evaluations = 20 quarterly evaluations/year, plus 5 annual computations integrated into the 1702RT/1702Q filings; 1 excess-credit register per credit-carrying entity
Owner: Tax Manager
Participants: Tax Accountant, CFO, Controller, External Tax Counsel, External Audit Team (provision audit), BIR (filings via eFPS)
Source: workflow W5530 — Minimum Corporate Income Tax (MCIT) Computation, Regime Evaluation &amp; 3-Year Excess-Credit Carry-Forward</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5530_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5530_Lane1" name="Tax Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5530_Lane2" name="Tax Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5530_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5530_Start4" name="Quarterly close (W9A) and the annual income-tax-return cycle (W407/W90 calendar); an…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5530_Task5" name="Gross-income base preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Gross-income base preparation: per entity, compute the MCIT base — gross income (gross receipts less sales returns, allowances and discounts, plus cost of goods sold where applicable) — with documentary support for each deduction assembled at the W9A cut-off
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: 1.5 hours per entity per quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5530_Task6" name="Quarterly MCIT vs normal-tax comparison">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quarterly MCIT vs normal-tax comparison: compute 2% MCIT on the base and compare against the normal corporate income tax per entity; pay and accrue the higher amount within the W590 provision and the W407 current-tax computation; file through the W260/eFPS quarterly cycle (1702Q)
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: inside the 1.5-hour quarterly cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5530_Task7" name="Annual computation &amp; return integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual computation &amp; return integration: annual MCIT determination per entity; reconcile to the W407 annual current-tax provision; confirm the final position on the 1702RT/1702Q filings with eFPS confirmations archived
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: ~4 hours per entity per year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5530_Task8" name="Excess-credit register">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Excess-credit register: where MCIT exceeds normal tax, record the excess per entity in the carry-forward register — amount, origin year, and expiry (creditable against normal income tax for the 3 immediately following taxable years); apply credits in order and flag lapsing credits 12 months ahead
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: ~2 hours per credit-carrying entity per year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5530_Task9" name="Relief evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Relief evaluation: where a loss year or business reversal drives MCIT above normal tax, assess the one-time relief options with External Tax Counsel and document the position taken
Responsible (R): Tax Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: event-driven; ≈ 8 hours/year budgeted</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5530_Task10" name="Documentation &amp; audit support">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Documentation &amp; audit support: maintain the MCIT workpapers (base support, computations, register) in the W256 retention structure; fold the papers into the W351/W95 provision-audit package and the BIR-examination evidence per W77
Responsible (R): Tax Accountant
Accountable (A): Tax Manager
Duration: ≈ 12 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5530_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5530_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5530_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5530_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-291 (ensure controlled execution — Tax &amp; Statutory (PA-17.3).) | - operational: quarterly MCIT-vs-normal-tax comparison signed off by the Tax Manager before the W590 provision posts | - operational: excess-credit register movements require Tax Manager review; lapsed credits require CFO acknowledgment
Owner: Tax Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5530_Assoc13" sourceRef="W5530_Annotation12" targetRef="W5530_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow14" sourceRef="W5530_Start4" targetRef="W5530_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow15" sourceRef="W5530_Task5" targetRef="W5530_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow16" sourceRef="W5530_Task6" targetRef="W5530_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow17" sourceRef="W5530_Task7" targetRef="W5530_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow18" sourceRef="W5530_Task8" targetRef="W5530_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow19" sourceRef="W5530_Task9" targetRef="W5530_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5530_Flow20" sourceRef="W5530_Task10" targetRef="W5530_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W5530_diag">
